## What is JSX?
JSX stands for JavaScript XML.
JSX is a syntax extension for JavaScript that allows us to write HTML-like code inside JavaScript.
It makes React code easier to read and write.

1. Example without JSX

import React from "react";

function App() {
  return React.createElement(
    "h1",
    null,
    "Hello React!"
  );
}

export default App;


2. Example with JSX

function App() {
  return (
    <h1>Hello React!</h1>
  );
}

export default App;

Both examples create the same heading.